<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43413" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sĕmĕlē</span></b> ,
			ēs (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sĕmĕla</span></b> , ae, pure Lat.
		collat. form in the cass. obll.), f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σεμέλη,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a daughter of
				Cadmus</i>, <i>and mother of Bacchus by Jupiter;
				nom.</i> Semele, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 3, 293</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. F. 6,
				485</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Tr. 4, 3, 67</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Am. 3,
				3, 37</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab. 167</span></i> and 179; <i>gen.</i> Semelae, <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 6,
				503</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Semeles,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 1, 19, 2</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Tib. 3, 4, 45</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 3,
				274</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 278</span></i>; dat. Semelae,
				<i><span class="en">Prop.
				2, 28</span></i> (3, 24), 27; acc. Semelen, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 3,
				261</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. F. 3, 715</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Semelam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 1, 12</span></i>
			; abl. Semelā, <i><span class="en">Cic. Tusc.
				1, 12, 28</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. N. D. 2, 24, 62</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Prop. 2,
			30</span></i> (3, 28), 29: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Semele,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab. 179</span></i>
			.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sĕmĕlēïus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to Semele</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">proles,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Bacchus</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					3, 520</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">5, 329</span></i>; <i><span class="en">9, 640</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thyoneus,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Bacchus</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 1, 17, 22</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sĕmĕlēus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of Semele</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">busta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 10, 903</span></i>
			.</div>
